WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 2 Student Video
Unit 1, Lesson 2: Faith

1
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.860
In college, I had a chance to be a resident assistant, a rep in charge of fun

2
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.300
activities and events on a floor.

3
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.340
Well, to help us have some compassion and understanding for students on our floor

4
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:24.460
who might have handicaps, the leadership decided that we would go around for a day

5
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.200
with a handicap of sorts. And my handicap was to wear a blindfold.

6
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.240
It really dawned on me for the first time since I had to go to the cafeteria, had to

7
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.580
go to class with this blindfold on, how tough it is to navigate life without sight.

8
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.660
Well, how did I cope? How did I make it through the day?

9
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.920
Well, I had to ask somebody to help me.

10
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.200
Who did I ask? I didn't ask a stranger.

11
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.160
I didn't ask somebody I just met.

12
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.720
I asked somebody I trusted, one of my basketball teammates, to help me out through

13
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.760
the day. People often have the idea that faith is blind.

14
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.940
And when it comes to issues of religion, it's like we're frolicking around, in the

15
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.700
dark, and basing our beliefs on sheer ignorance.

16
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.920
Well, this might be true for some religions, but it is not true for Christianity.

17
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:19.280
You see, biblically, faith is trusting what we have reason to believe is

18
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:25.200
true. Just as I followed the guidance of my friend, whom I had good reason to

19
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.820
trust when I was blindfolded, God asks us to follow Him, and He's given us good

20
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.960
reasons to trust Him.

21
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.570
We are not called to blind faith.

22
00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:50.490
We see a remarkable pattern in Exodus, chapter 7 through 14.

23
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:56.250
God would do a powerful miracle through Moses, a sign which gave the people

24
00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:02.170
knowledge of who God is. And as a result, He called them to believe in Him and

25
00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.350
to place their trust in Him.

26
00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:08.910
So here's the pattern. God would do a miracle through Moses.

27
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:13.170
This gave the people knowledge, and then they were called to believe.

28
00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.710
Miracle, knowledge, belief. Consider an example.

29
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:23.190
In Exodus, chapter 7, verse 17, Moses is about to do the miracle of turning the

30
00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:26.810
water, the Nile, into blood. And it says,

31
00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:35.030
Now what is this? This is the miracle Moses was about to do.

32
00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:40.390
And it says, And you shall know, because that miracle would give them knowledge.

33
00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.370
So Moses is doing this powerful miracle.

34
00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.670
It gives them knowledge that the God of Israel is the one true God, and then they're

35
00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:53.850
called to belief. So our pattern, which is clearly emerging, is miracle,

36
00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.310
knowledge, and then belief.

37
00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.410
We see the same pattern in the New Testament, in the Gospel of Mark.

38
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.030
Jesus is in Capernaum, and He's preaching in a home.

39
00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.670
And four men bring a paralytic to Him.

40
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.310
And they can't get in to Him, so they go up on the roof, remove the roof, and lower

41
00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:19.230
this paralytic down to Jesus. And Jesus sees them, as a result of their faith, says,

42
00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:25.630
Now the scribes and Pharisees are thinking, Wait a minute, who can forgive sins

43
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.890
but God alone? This is blasphemy.

44
00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:33.230
What does Jesus do? If you skip down and look at verse 10, it says this, Jesus said,

45
00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:38.970
So that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth

46
00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.730
to forgive sins. He looks at the paralytic.

47
00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:42.330
He says,

48
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:51.550
Jesus did that sign as proof that gave them knowledge of who He was, and the

49
00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.990
implication was Jesus is the Son of God.

50
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.630
Now believe in Him.

51
00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.130
You might be thinking, Wait a minute.

52
00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:03.450
Didn't Jesus do the miracle because of the man's faith?

53
00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:09.650
After all, it says in Mark chapter 2 that Jesus, seeing their faith, pronounced to

54
00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:12.290
the man, Son, your sins are forgiven.

55
00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:17.910
Now it is true that God often does reward our faith by performing miracles.

56
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.990
But let's ask a more basic question.

57
00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:24.950
Why did these four men and the paralytic come to Jesus in the first place?

58
00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:29.790
And the answer is because, as Mark 1 tells us, Jesus had already been performing

59
00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.750
miracles. Jesus had already been casting out demons.

60
00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.870
He had given them evidence and signs that He's the Son of God.

61
00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:42.190
So they came to Him with confidence and put a faith in Him that was well placed.

62
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:47.590
Jesus calls people to love God with their heart, with their soul, with their

63
00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:52.470
strength, and with their minds. In the Old Testament, God says, through the prophet

64
00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.850
Isaiah, Come, let us reason together.

65
00:04:56.330 --> 00:05:01.070
In the Old Testament and in the New Testament, God calls people to an intelligent

66
00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.510
faith. And He still does the same today.

67
00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:10.070
This is why in the Gospel of John, a gospel which is written recording the miracles

68
00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:14.050
of Jesus, and inviting people to come to Him, and inviting people to a confident

69
00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:19.830
faith. At the very end of the Gospel, John writes in chapter 20, verses 30

70
00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:25.670
through 31, that Jesus has performed many other miracles not even recorded

71
00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:31.330
in this book. But they've been recorded so we might have confidence that Jesus is

72
00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.070
the Son of God. He's the Christ.

73
00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:37.190
And by believing in Him, we may experience eternal life.

74
00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:43.370
The Gospel of John is written so we understand who Jesus is, based on the miracles,

75
00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:49.090
so we can have a confident faith, and by having that faith, experience eternal life.

76
00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:55.170
Biblical faith is not blind. The Bible invites non-believers to

77
00:05:55.170 --> 00:06:01.170
investigate the evidence, to consider the claims of Christ, and then to consider

78
00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:06.050
believing in Him. And as Christians, we're also not called to a blind faith.

79
00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:11.050
We are called to think deeply about our faith, to know why we believe what we

80
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:16.750
believe, we are called to have an answer when people ask us the reason for the hope

81
00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.010
we have within.

